cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sigma-GLYPH: a portable deterministic check engine with size-priced budgets"
abstract: >-
  A content-addressed computation core: given the same term hash, uint32 budget
  and valid partial content store, implementations return the same canonical
  result and reported spend, with no clock or network in reduction. One budget
  bounds priced actions and peak semantic materialized-node count; it does not by
  itself bound process RSS, stack, storage or allocator overhead, and a verifier
  still needs a local admission limit. Determinism, totality, semantic size and
  store-monotonicity properties are mechanised in Lean 4. Three implementations
  from one author/model lineage agree on every conformance vector. A
  wave/coordinate layer sits above identity and never inside it.
message: "If you use or evaluate this work, please cite it."
